Package: stringzilla-cli
Version: ${VERSION}
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: ${ARCH}
Installed-Size: ${INSTALLED_SIZE}
Maintainer: Ash Vardanian <1983160+ashvardanian@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ashvardanian/StringZilla-CLI
Description: SIMD-accelerated command-line text processing utilities
 Drop-in accelerated replacements for common text tools: sz-find, sz-replace,
 sz-sort, sz-count, sz-dedup, sz-rows, sz-cols, sz-split, sz-segment-utf8 and
 sz-sha256.
 Each binary dispatches at load time to the widest SIMD tier the running CPU
 supports, so one package serves every machine of this architecture.
 .
 Statically linked against musl, so it depends on no system library.
